pointed by the President\nfrom knowledgeable representatives in health care practice and complemen-\ntary and alternative medicine. The President shall designate a Chair from\namong the members of the Commission. The Secretary of Health and Human\nServices (Secretary) shall appoint an Executive Director for the Commission.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 1","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec1","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"Sec. 2. Functions. The Commission shall provide a report, through the\nSecretary, to the President on legislative and administrative recommendations\nfor assuring that public policy maximizes the benefits to Americans of\ncomplementary and alternative medicine. The recommendations shall address\nthe following:","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2 (lead-in)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec2","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) the education and training of health care practitioners in complementary\nand alternative medicine;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(a)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec2(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) coordinated research to increase knowledge about complementary and\nalternative medicine practices and products;","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(b)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec2(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) the provision to health care professionals of reliable and useful informa-\ntion about complementary and alternative medicine that can be made readily\naccessible and understandable to the general public; and","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(c)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec2(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) guidance for appropriate access to and delivery of complementary\nand alternative medicine.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 2(d)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec2(d)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(a) To the extent permitted by law, the heads of\nexecutive departments and agencies shall provide the Commission, upon\nrequest, with such information and assistance as it may require for the\npurpose of carrying out its functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(a)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec3(a)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(b) Each member of the Commission shall receive compensation at a\nrate equal to the daily equivalent of the annual rate specified for Level\n1V of the Executive Schedule (5 U.S.C. 5315) for each day during which\nthe member is engaged in the performance of the duties of the Commission.\nWhile away from their homes or regular places of business in the performance\nof the duties of the Commission, members shall be allowed travel expenses,\nincluding per diem in lieu of subsistence, as authorized by law for persons\nserving intermittently in Government service (5 U.S.C. 5701–5707).","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(b)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec3(b)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(c) The Department shall provide the Commission with funding and with\nadministrative services, facilities, staff, and other support services necessary\nfor the performance of the Commission’s functions.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(c)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec3(c)","state_at_cutoff":null},{"current_predicate":null,"first_end":null,"later_events":[],"original_operative_text":"(d) In accordance with guidelines issued by the Administrator of General\nServices, the Secretary shall perform the functions of the President under\nthe Federal Advisory Committee Act, as amended (5 U.S.C. App.), with\nrespect to the Commission, except that of reporting to the Congress.\nVerDate 07<MAR>2000 18:45 Mar 09, 2000 Jkt 190000 PO 00000 Frm 00003 Fmt 4705 Sfmt 4790 E:\\FR\\FM\\10MRE0.SGM pfrm08 PsN: 10MRE0\n=== PDF page 2 of 2 ===\n13234 Federal Register / Vol. 65, No. 48 / Friday, March 10, 2000 / Presidential Documents\n(e) The Commission shall terminate 2 years from the date of this order\nunless extended by the President prior to such date.","original_source":{"page_or_item":"65 FR 13233, PDF pages 1-2; Sec. 3(d)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"scope_id":"EO:13147#sec3(d)","state_at_cutoff":null}],"original_representation":{"page_or_item":"whole per-document Federal Register PDF (65 FR 13233)","sha256":"a7ec60f5bdd77be4da2ba094a3c7c7bc6fedfef6c845192765bd7fb80ec2a034","url":"https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2000-03-10/pdf/00-6126.pdf"},"research_rationale":"","savings_residuals":null,"schema":"eo-lifecycle-claim/v1","unresolved_material_gaps":["DRAFT: state_at_cutoff not decided for 10 clause(s); clause inventory completeness not confirmed","DRAFT: whole-order ending not established","DRAFT: savings and residual effects not closed","DRAFT: later_source_search not recorded (machine searches are proposals only; paste them after judging them adequate and resolving every CONFLICT line)"],"whole_order_end":null,"whole_order_status":"no"},"draft_schema":"eo-claim-draft/v1","instrument_id":"EO:13147"}
